      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd1w",
          "text": "In Denver, common motorcycle accident injuries often include head and brain trauma, spinal cord damage, broken bones, severe abrasions, and internal harm. These injuries range from minor to catastrophic, frequently requiring emergency care, surgeries, and long-term rehabilitation. The National Safety Council reports that helmets are a critical safeguard against fatal head injuries, reducing the risk of death by 37% and head injury by 69%.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
