      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd26",
          "text": "Most Common Types of Injuries Caused by Motorcycle Accidents",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bd2b",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd28",
          "text": "The nature of injuries in a motorcycle crash often depends on the point of impact, the speed of travel, the size and weight of other vehicles involved, and whether riders wore protective gear. The ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd29",
          "text": "most common types of motorcycle accident injuries",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2a",
          "text": " include (and are not limited to):",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bd2e",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2c",
          "text": "Head and Brain Injuries",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2d",
          "text": " – Concussions and traumatic brain injuries (TBIs) are frequent due to the lack of a protective vehicle frame. Even helmeted riders can suffer lasting neurological harm in high-speed impacts.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bd2h",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2f",
          "text": "Spinal Cord Injuries",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2g",
          "text": " – Severe crashes may cause partial or total paralysis, while less extreme trauma can result in chronic pain and limited mobility.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bd2k",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2i",
          "text": "Fractures",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2j",
          "text": " – Arms, legs, collarbones, and ribs are often broken when riders are thrown or struck.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bd2n",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2l",
          "text": "Road Rash",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2m",
          "text": " – Abrasions from sliding across pavement may require skin grafts.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bd2q",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2o",
          "text": "Internal Injuries",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd2p",
          "text": " – Organ damage or bleeding can be fatal if untreated.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
